{"run_id": "split-one-4403-s03-d216ce", "t": 7.684, "type": "model_call", "step": 6, "purpose": null, "model": "gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "latency_s": 3.411, "usage": {"input_tokens": 373, "output_tokens": 399, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2176, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 2549}, "cost_usd": 0.0076425, "tool_calls": [{"name": "return_finding", "input": {"result": {"issue": 4403, "label": "feature", "file": "src/export/csv.ts", "evidence": "CSV exports in src/export/csv.ts include a BOM by design, as set by default in CsvOptions. This allows spreadsheet apps to detect UTF-8 encoding."}, "status": "found", "searched": ["issue-4403", "CSV export", "export", "BOM"], "not_searched": [], "calls_used": 5, "could_not_determine": []}}], "tools": ["issues_read", "code_search", "code_read_file", "return_finding"], "request": null, "text": "The issue #4403 inquires about whether the presence of a byte order mark (BOM) at the start of CSV exports is intentional. Upon investigation, the file `src/export/csv.ts` is responsible for the CSV export logic. In this file, there is a clear implementation of BOM usage. By default, the BOM is included unless specified otherwise via the `bom` option in the `CsvOptions` interface. The comment explains that spreadsheet applications use the BOM to detect UTF-8 encoding when a CSV is opened directly. Therefore, the inclusion of the BOM is a deliberate feature, and the code allows for it to be turned off by setting the `bom` option to `false`.\n\n```typescript\n// src/export/csv.ts\nexport interface CsvOptions {\n  columns?: readonly ExportColumn[];\n  /** Prefix a byte order mark. On by default. */\n  bom?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst BOM = \"\ufeff\";\n\nexport function writeCsv(rows: readonly ReportRow[], options: CsvOptions = {}): ExportFile {\n  const { columns = COLUMN_ORDER, bom = true } = options;\n  const text = toDelimited(rows, columns);\n  return {\n    body: Buffer.from(bom ? BOM + text : text, \"utf8\"),\n    contentType: CONTENT_TYPES.csv,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nThis confirms that the BOM presence in CSV exports is intentional and part of the design. \n\nI will return this finding with the appropriate classification.", "agent": "investigator-4403", "parent": "coordinator"}
